course: dictionary
lesson: 603
title: Knowing what is around you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aware means you know about something, or you notice it. You can be aware of a feeling, a sound, a danger or a problem. «Be aware of your surroundings» means use your eyes and ears to notice what is near you.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Being aware means using your eyes and ears to know what is happening around you, so that you spot trouble early and have time to act.» The words know, spot and early tell you that aware means noticing things in time to do something about them.
explain: Aware usually comes after a verb, such as «be aware», «was aware» or «make someone aware». «Make someone aware» means tell them, so they now know about something. «Well aware» means you know it very clearly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you put «knowing about» in place of aware, and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Aware means knowing about something or noticing it.
fact: «Be aware of your surroundings» means watch and listen, especially near roads, water or strangers.
fact: Aware often comes after a verb, as in «be aware», «was aware» or «make someone aware».
fact: «Make someone aware» means to tell them, so that they know about something.
fact: Someone who is aware understands what is happening around them and what matters, such as being environmentally aware or safety aware.
exercise: «Being aware means using your eyes and ears to know what is happening around you.» What does aware mean? | Running very fast | Hiding from other people | *Knowing about what is happening around you | Fast asleep and dreaming
exercise: In a safety lesson, what does «be aware of your surroundings» mean? | Ignore everything around you | Shout as loudly as you can | Close your eyes and rest | *Watch and listen, especially near roads, water or strangers
exercise: Why do you need to be aware near a busy road? | So you can forget where you are | *So you spot danger early and have time to act | So you can go faster than the cars | So you can close your eyes
test: Ella says aware is just a fancy word for asleep. What does aware really mean? | *Knowing about something or noticing it | Angry with someone | Fast asleep | Ready to leave
test: In «The teacher made the class aware of the storm warning», what does made aware mean? | Gave them a prize | Sent them home early | Made them go quiet | *Told them so they knew about the warning
exam: Which phrase is about watching and listening near a road? | *Be aware of your surroundings | Close your eyes at the kerb | Run across the road quickly | Be unaware and walk on
